From baf8145e24fd5baacf02b465f16c89f6e9b03e57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jatniel <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:08:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show the profile picker from the title screen (iOS)

A new Mode::Profiles screen, reached from a small "P" button next to the
title's icon buttons (iOS only, so desktop layout is untouched). It lists
the profiles, selects rows by tap, and creates, renames, deletes and picks
the profile for the next launch. profile::running() tells the screen which
profile this run is in, so the running one can't be deleted.

Choosing a profile only records it for the next launch; moving the running
game into it is the next change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
